### Opti class
- derivative of asb.Opti
- used to generate problem-wide interfaces and handles interface with CASADi

### Physics Model
- specifies the x,u variables and the relationship with rigid motion. So forces from the aerodynamics model (described later) create forces in the body frame which become accelerations, then velocities, then positions based on relationships determined here
- also handles specific rotations and transformations of the model
- how specific controls are modeled (like aielron, flap, throttle)

### Aerodynamics Model
- Forcing modelf(x,u) that creates forces that move the point mass
- ingests the point mass model and creates the relationships that determine $\dot{x}$
- needs to use all variables


### Wind Model 
- generates the wind velocity $V_w(x,z)$ based on user construction
- has ability to overlay gusts at different directions and different types of gusts
- currently only implemented as a gaussian, but is not restricted to that

